From a02c8d6b21bb16cb89a76b8823fd418ec4a2655f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ugo Mignon <56931733+TartanLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:15:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(appicon): support single-size app icons

Xcode 14+ writes an appiconset with one 1024x1024 universal entry
(platform "ios", no idiom, no scale). The loader rejected it because
the entry had no scale.

Decode idiom as optional and generate the iPhone, iPad and store sizes
from the master with an area-averaging downscaler, then reuse the
multi-size path. The master must be exactly 1024x1024. Dark and tinted
entries are skipped, other platforms are rejected.

Also set the rendition key's icon index from the point size, as actool
does, so icons of the same idiom and scale no longer share a key, and
drop duplicate loose file names.
